.TH SENEMOS-NABU-COLOR-PROFILE 1 "7 September 2026" "SENEMOS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
senemos-nabu-color-profile \- convert authorized Nabu QDCM calibration to ICC
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B senemos-nabu-color-profile catalog
.br
.B senemos-nabu-color-profile import
.I qdcm.xml
[
.BI --output-dir= directory
]
.br
.B senemos-nabu-color-profile validate
.I profile.icc
.br
.B senemos-nabu-color-profile apply
.RB { srgb | display-p3 }
[
.BI --panel= revision
]
[
.BI --profile-dir= directory
]
[
.BI --output= connector
]
[
.B --dry-run
]
.br
.B senemos-nabu-color-profile auto
[
.BI --profile-dir= directory
]
[
.BI --output= connector
]
[
.BI --marker= path
]
[
.BI --retries= count
]
[
.B --dry-run
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B senemos-nabu-color-profile
creates ICC v4 RGB display profiles for KDE KWin from a locally supplied,
authorized Xiaomi Pad 5 QDCM XML. The proprietary source XML is not copied or
installed. Generated profiles default to
.IR ~/.local/share/icc/senemos/nabu .
.PP
The static Android HAL sRGB and Display P3 SDR modes are supported. Native,
content-aware, PA-v2 video and HDR modes are intentionally excluded because
they cannot be represented faithfully by this conversion path.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B catalog
List supported and deliberately excluded Android modes.
.TP
.BI import " qdcm.xml"
Generate separate sRGB and Display P3 ICC profiles for the panel revision
encoded in the authorized XML filename.
.TP
.BI validate " profile.icc"
Check display class, RGB/XYZ spaces, required tags and KWin-compatible
BToA 33x33x33 LUTs.
.TP
.BI apply " profile"
Validate and apply a generated SDR profile to the enabled internal DSI output
through kscreen-doctor.
.TP
.B auto
Read the kernel's Nabu panel revision, falling back to the read-only UEFI panel
configuration on older kernels, then select the matching packaged sRGB ICC for
the current user. An existing packaged sRGB or Display P3 choice is
kept on the correct panel variant. Custom profiles and later user overrides
are preserved. If neither source exposes a supported revision, no display
setting is changed.
.SH SAFETY
Use
.B --dry-run
before applying a profile. Panel revision and physical color accuracy still
require device-side verification with a colorimeter. The generated profile is
an experimental conversion of the documented IGC, fine 3D LUT and GC stages,
not proof of pixel-for-pixel equivalence with Android's proprietary display
HAL.
.PP
KWin calls only EDID-derived colorimetry "Built-in". The Nabu DSI panel has no
EDID, and choosing that source would not execute the factory 3D LUT. The tool
therefore uses KWin's ICC source instead of presenting a false built-in state.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/icc/senemos/nabu
Default output and lookup directory for generated profiles.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/senemos-nabu/color-profile-auto.json
Per-user state recording whether automatic selection still owns the setting.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kscreen-doctor (1)
